The comment in the code explicitly mentions runtime class assertions, which rely on the API structure being correctly placed in the `.dev_apis` linker section. A failure in this placement would lead to a crash when the device's API pointer is validated.

Removing the redundant `static` keyword is the correct fix to ensure the API structure is defined correctly and placed in the appropriate linker section, resolving the runtime crash.

